Z||000003||theogre||09-08-2001||01:46 PM||||The forum could probably handle that but it would be better to put something that large into a web page that is static someplace. A static page allows better management of that many pictures. It will also load faster since people will only have 3-4 pictures on a page instead of waiting for the forum to try to caugh up such a gigantic page. Remember, we still have a large portion of modem users here.<P>If you do put it here, use the PIP software so the images are on cliff's server. that way the images will become permanent parts of the archives. Pictures that have been hosted on third party equipement have had a habbit of vanishing when people wanted to see them later.<P>If you put it here, I'd strongly recomend some image editing to get the file size of the images as small as posible. For web use you can drop image resolution to 96 DPI and they will still look good. That one step will drop file size tremendously.<P>If you aren't up to doing a whole article, I have room in the project area in my cave. E-mail me for more details if you want to do that.||||reg||1
